# PART 21: DATABASE SCHEMA AND DOCUMENT RELATIONSHIPS

Create a documented, consistent Firestore schema based on the existing application.

A possible starting structure is:

`users/{uid}`

Stores the user's authorized profile and role.

`courses/{courseId}`

Stores the course and its lecturer ownership.

`courses/{courseId}/enrollments/{uid}`

Stores the student's enrolment in that course.

`courses/{courseId}/announcements/{announcementId}`

Stores announcements for that course.

`courses/{courseId}/resources/{resourceId}`

Stores published learning-resource metadata.

`courses/{courseId}/assignments/{assignmentId}`

Stores assignment information.

`courses/{courseId}/assignments/{assignmentId}/submissions/{submissionId}`

Stores submission metadata and grading status.

`courses/{courseId}/quizzes/{quizId}`

Stores published assessment information.

`courses/{courseId}/quizzes/{quizId}/attempts/{attemptId}`

Stores assessment attempts and their status.

`courses/{courseId}/attendanceSessions/{sessionId}`

Stores attendance-session metadata.

`courses/{courseId}/attendanceSessions/{sessionId}/records/{uid}`

Stores attendance for the relevant student.

`courses/{courseId}/gradeRecords/{uid}`

Stores or summarizes the authorized student's course results where appropriate.

`courses/{courseId}/meetings/{meetingId}`

Stores live-meeting metadata.

`users/{uid}/budgetPlans/{planId}`

Stores the user's budget plans.

`users/{uid}/periodTracker/{recordId}`

Stores the user's private period-tracker records.

You may refine this structure when needed, but document the final structure and why it is appropriate.

Use stable document IDs and explicit relationships. Avoid depending on array indexes or arbitrary browser-generated numeric IDs.

Use Firestore transactions or batched writes where multiple operations must remain consistent.

Use server timestamps for important official records.

Create required Firestore indexes.

Design queries around the actual dashboard and course workflows. Do not load the entire database into the browser.

